<title>POLAND: Polish yr/yr PPI 9.6 pct in May vs 9.8 April.</title>
<headline>Polish yr/yr PPI 9.6 pct in May vs 9.8 April.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish producer prices rose 0.4 percent in May against a 0.6 percent rise in April, taking year-on-year producer price inflation down to 9.6 percent, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said.</p>
<p>It said PPI rose 4.1 percent in the January-May period.  </p>
<p> POLISH PRODUCER INFLATION	     MAY     APRIL	MAY 96</p>
<p> month/month change (pct)		0.4	0.6	  0.6</p>
<p> yr/yr change (pct)			9.6	9.8	 13.9</p>
<p>  manufacturing m/m change	     0.4	0.5 (0.6)  0.7</p>
<p>  manufacturing yr/yr change	   8.2	8.5 (8.6) 10.5</p>
<p>  mining m/m change			0.4	2.2 (1.5) -0.8</p>
<p>  mining yr/yr change		   18.0     16.7(15.8) 12.5</p>
<p>  utilities m/m change		   0.1	0.3 (0.2)  0.3</p>
<p>  utilities yr/yr change		 9.3     11.2(11.1) 18.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures in brackets were revised.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
